      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, Media and Communication, AY 2025-2026 -",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, Media and Communication, AY 2025-2026 - Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, Media and Communication, AY 2025-2026 - Kiosk mode Join our team Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, Media and Communication, AY 2025-2026 Adjunct Faculty Evening - Continuing Education, Media and Communication, AY 2025-2026 492786 487 - Communications Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Closing on: Oct 8 2029 On-site $1,610 - $1,987 per SHCI (Semester Hours of Credit Instruction) Overview: Salem State University is seeking adjunct professors with interest and experience teaching Media and Communication. Teaching assignments will include multimedia story telling, media literacy and writing for media. Other subjects will depend upon the expertise of the candidate and needs of the program. Duties and Responsibilities: Work collaboratively with faculty, in a school with future-directed leadership and a collective focus on academic excellence, success of our students and faculty development. Required Qualifications: Master's degree Teaching experience Demonstrated commitment to collaboration and collegiality Demonstrated commitment to teaching, supervision, and advising Strength and potential for excellence and leadership in community engagement and university services Preferred Qualifications: Appropriate terminal degree College-level teaching experience, at both the undergraduate and graduate levels Experience teaching a multicultural population Working Location: This can be onsite position in Salem, MA with some on-campus, in-person responsibilities or online or hybrid models may be considered. Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and transcripts. To ensure you are assigned the highest eligible rank, you should provide the total sum of credits you have taught at the college/university level. This information can be added to your CV, cover letter, or a separate document. E