    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-director-of-outreach-and-community-engagement": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement -",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement - Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement - Kiosk mode Join our team Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $80,000 Overview The School of Social Work at Salem State University seeks a dynamic, strategic, and experienced professional to join our School as the Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement. You will play a pivotal role in leading the expansion of our innovative BSW and MSW online degree pathways. This is a leadership role designed for a project management expert who can bridge the gap between academic rigor and workforce needs. As the primary architect of our outreach strategy, you will build and sustain high-impact partnerships with community and traditional colleges, regional employers, and diverse stakeholders to create seamless educational pipelines for the next generation of social work professionals. In this role, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the next generation of social work professionals through accessible, equitable, and efficient pathways. The MSW program admitted its first online cohort in January of 2022 and the BSW program admitted its first cohort in May 2025. The role is a staff position, does not include teaching responsibilities, is not eligible for remote work and is not eligible for tenure. The Assistant Director for Outreach and Community Engagement reports to the Associate Dean. The School of Social Work offers both an MSW and BSW education to approximately 500 students. The MSW program admitted its first online cohort in January of 2022 and the BSW program admitted its first cohort in May 2025. . Salem State University values, celebrates and appreciates diversity in all its forms and endeavors to create a space that reflects the campus community population which it serves. Our students come to Salem State University from 38 states and 48 countries and reflect the demographics of the greater Boston community in which we live. We are passionate about providing an experience for them and our fellow staff and faculty, where everyone can feel supported while they explore, learn, and celebrate their identities, similarities, and differences. We welcome you to come celebrate with us and become a member of our community. Please Note: This is a three-year, grant funded, full-time 12-month staff position, with an on-campus presence requirement. Required Qualifications 1. Master’s degree in Social Work from an accredited institution. 2. Minimum of two years of documented post-graduate social work practice experience. 3. Demonstrated experience in project management. 4. A valid driver's License Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience working in higher education. 2. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite of products. 3. Networking, outreach, and team-building skills. 4. Demonstrated problem-solving and organizational skills with the flexibility to manage multiple tasks. 5. Ability to interpret and apply rules, regulations, policies and procedures. 6. Strong interpersonal and presentation skills, including experience working in teams and the ability to navigate various team dynamics and work directly with stakeholders. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 4f330704 Last Name (required) 3f731083 Email (required) 99d09d2c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493091 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) dfecdfee Last Name (required) a5a3e9bc Email (required) 0abe3395 Job Alert d30c456f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 243 - School Of Social Work 243 - School Of Social Work Categories Staff: Administrator/Professional Staff: Administrator/P