    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-computer-science-software-engineering-and-cloud-computing-full-time-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track -",
      "description": "Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track On-site $80,000 - $85,000 Overview The Department of Computer Science at Salem State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the open rank, beginning in Fall 2027. We particularly welcome candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: cloud computing, software engineering, and databases. The successful candidate will demonstrate a forward-looking vision for the computing field, a strong commitment to effective teaching and student learning in a four-year undergraduate program, and excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Teaching responsibilities will include introductory, intermediate, and advanced courses in computer science and information technology, including courses within one or more of the preferred areas of specialization. The candidate will also be expected to contribute to departmental and university service and to maintain an active program of scholarly or professional development appropriate to the position and rank. Salem State University is where scholarship meets purpose. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University, we believe education matters beyond the classroom, and our faculty are central to that mission. They bring intellectual curiosity and a genuine commitment to student success, teaching students who will go on to shape their communities, many of whom are the first in their families to earn a college degree. We value collaboration, academic rigor, and the kind of civic-minded engagement that makes a real difference. If you're driven by meaningful work and want to be part of something bigger than any single course or semester, Salem State is your place. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract. Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship, and contributions to the continuous improvement of the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications: PhD in computer science or a closely related field. ABD with a master’s degree in computer science or a closely related field are welcome to apply. Conferral is required by May 2027. Experience in teaching introductory, intermediate-level, and advanced-level computer science and information technology courses. Experience applying the latest computing technologies into the curriculum. Innovative approaches to teaching one or more of the following: cloud computing, software engineering, and databases. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in teaching upper-level computer science and information technology courses. Professional applied experience in computer science/information technology, in general, and cloud computing, software engineering, and databases, in particular. Demonstrated ability and willingness to apply innovative approaches and the latest applied teaching experience; and experience in and a commitment to teaching in a multicultural, multiracial environment with students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles. Working Location: This is an on-site position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests, please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, unofficial transcripts, teaching statement, and research statement. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. All applicants are encouraged to apply; however, Salem State University cannot guarantee that it will sponsor visas for individuals who are not otherwise authorized to work in the United States. EEO Statement: The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests, please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies: Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 71971f6a Last Name (required) 7f643443 Email (required) 43e98be6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493091 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 3dd735dd Last Name (required) 941fb2be Email (required) b3857a01 Job Alert aaa8df54 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 140 - Computer Science Dept 140 - Computer Science Dept Categories Faculty: Tenured Faculty: Tenured Employment Type Tenure-Track Tenure-Track Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) a158c612 Last Name (required) d543d5ae Email (required) 1fe64111 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Performance Cookies Performance cookies are cookies used specifically for gathering data on how visitors use a website, which pages of a website are visited most often, or if they get error messages on web pages. These cookies monitor only the performance of the site as the user interacts with it. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a working location"
