    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-computer-science-ai-and-machine-learning-full-time-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track -",
      "description": "Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty: Computer Science, (AI and Machine Learning), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493091 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track On-site $90,000-$95,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Overview The of Computer Science department at Salem State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the open rank, beginning in Fall 2027. We particularly welcome candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Robotics. The successful candidate will demonstrate a forward-looking vision for the computing field, a strong commitment to effective teaching and student learning in a four-year undergraduate program, and excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Teaching responsibilities will include introductory, intermediate, and advanced courses in computer science and information technology, including courses within one or more of the preferred areas of specialization. The candidate will also be expected to contribute to departmental and university service and to maintain an active program of scholarly or professional development appropriate to the position and rank. What makes Salem State University distinctive isn't just what happens in our classrooms. It's who's in them. Our students are ambitious, diverse and often the first in their families to pursue higher education. Our faculty rise to meet that with rigorous scholarship, thoughtful teaching and a genuine investment in student growth. We're the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University and a proud Hispanic and Minority-Serving Institution, designations we've earned and take seriously. If you're looking for a collegial academic home where your work truly matters, Salem State delivers. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours (approximately 4 lecture or lab sections) per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications PhD in computer science or a closely related field. ABD with a master’s degree in computer science or a closely related field are welcome to apply. Conferral is required by May 2027. Experience teaching introductory, intermediate-level, and advanced-level computer science and information technology courses. Experience applying the latest computing technologies into the curriculum. Innovative approaches to teaching one or more of the following: artificial intelligence, machine learning, and robotics. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching upper-level computer science and information technology courses. Professional applied experience in computer science/information technology, in general, and artificial intelligence, machine learning, and robotics, in particular. Demonstrated ability and willingness to apply innovative approaches and the latest applied teaching experience; and experience in and a commitment to teaching in a multicultural, multiracial environment with students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, unofficial transcripts, and research statement. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. All applicants are encouraged to apply; however, Salem State University cannot guarantee that it will sponsor visas for individuals who are not otherwise authorized to work in the United States. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 25212562 Last Name (required) 039efe0e Email (required) f3f6b984 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 3229f172 Last Name (required) 2be3047b Email (required) 87578f28 Job Alert 2b1527f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each drop