    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/small-group-trainer": {
      "title": "Small Group Trainer -",
      "description": "Small Group Trainer - Small Group Trainer - Kiosk mode Join our team Small Group Trainer Small Group Trainer 493001 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Faculty: Temporary/Contract Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time On-site 0 Overview Individual will work with Gassett Fitness Center members of various age, gender, and ability levels. Individual must hold an accredited personal training certification and will develop and lead small group training programs for the Department of Campus Life and Recreation. The number of program participants will range from 4-8 and program length will vary from 6-12 weeks. In this small group setting, trainers are required to motivate and educate participants on proper exercise techniques, set goals for the class/semester, and check in with participants. Trainers will be responsible for designing and implementing safe and effective programs, providing a motivating and enjoyable environment, and assisting participants with equipment set-up and use. Trainers must implement proper cuing and injury prevention practices. Trainers must have knowledge of fitness, endurance training, strength/power training and program design. Trainers must have a strong ability to coach and manage time, motivating multiple individuals in a group setting. Must have the desire and capacity to coach all fitness levels. A nationally accredited Personal Training certification/training is required. All trainers must hold and maintain current CPR/AED Certifications. All Trainers should attend relevant workshops, trainings, and conferences to obtain the number of continuing education credits (CECs) needed to maintain their current certifications and assist in their professional development. Required Qualifications Hold an accredited personal training certification Knowledge of fitness, endurance training, strength/power training and program design Strong ability to coach and manage time, motivating multiple individuals in a group setting Desire and capacity to coach all fitness levels Preferred Qualifications Current CPR/AED Certification or ability to obtain upon hire At least 1 year of personal training experience with group training responsibilities Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional/frequent/regular work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. // resume and cover letter. // Please apply online. Resume and cover letter are not required, but are appreciated. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) e68d07d4 Last Name (required) 1b134306 Email (required) ddb660fb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 49