    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-faculty-day-world-lang-cultures-and-education-ay-2026-2027": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 -",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 - Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 - Kiosk mode Join our team Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 Adjunct Faculty Day, World Lang & Cultures and Education, AY 2026-2027 493079 177 - World Languages / Cultures Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Hybrid $1,000 - $2,253.60 per Semester Hour Credit of Instruction Salem State University invites applications for a temporary Adjunct Professor of Spanish Education with a joint appointment in the Department of World Languages and Cultures and the McKeown School of Education for spring 2027. This position plays a central leadership role in the university’s Spanish teacher licensure programs. The candidate will teach Spanish teacher licensure courses for the 4+1 BA/MEd with Initial Licensure and the Master of Arts in Teaching (MAT) in Spanish. These programs are jointly supported by the Department of World Languages and Cultures and the McKeown School of Education. Teaching Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will be distributed across the two units and will focus primarily on licensure-related coursework, including but not limited to: • Spanish Methods I and II courses with integrated, co-requisite field experiences • Student teaching seminar and practicum • Advanced-track courses such as Action Research and Clinical sequences Service & Professional Engagement The candidate will be expected to: • Engage in service activities in both the Department of World Languages and Cultures and the McKeown School of Education • Collaborate across disciplines to align licensure curricula, assessment practices, and clinical expectations • Participate actively in state, regional, and national professional organizations related to world language education Working Location: This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with some on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and official transcripts. To ensure you are assigned the highest eligible rank, you should provide the total sum of credits you have taught at the college/university level. This information can be added to your CV, cover letter, or a separate document. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement: The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Apply now First Name (required) d3d61025 Last Name (required) 0f081bbd Email (required) f224730d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) d24b0734 Last Name (required) 454c5640 Email (required) fc49dae3 Job Alert 163fb3cd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning t