    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-biology-anatomy-and-physiology-biomedical-sciences-nursing-full-time-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Faculty: Biology, (Anatomy and Physiology - Biomedical Sciences Nursing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track -",
      "description": "Faculty: Biology, (Anatomy and Physiology - Biomedical Sciences Nursing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Faculty: Biology, (Anatomy and Physiology - Biomedical Sciences Nursing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Biology, (Anatomy and Physiology - Biomedical Sciences Nursing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty: Biology, (Anatomy and Physiology - Biomedical Sciences Nursing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 492979 121 - Biology Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Overview The Biology Department at Salem State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure track faculty position in biomedical sciences to begin September 2027. We seek a colleague who encourages student learning through innovative pedagogy who has expertise in anatomy and physiology, pathology, immunology, or related field. The successful candidate will have primary teaching responsibility in Anatomy and Physiology I and II and the opportunity to teach upper-level electives in our catalog (e.g. Human Anatomy, Human Physiology, General Pathology, Endocrinology, Immunology) and/or introductory biology courses for nonmajors. We seek a colleague interested in taking an active role in the Pre-Health Advising Committee and providing guidance to students pursuing careers in medical sciences. The ideal candidate will have plans for engaging undergraduate students in course-based and/or mentored research opportunities. We seek a collaborative colleague who cares deeply about supporting students and preparing future scientists and STEM professionals. Biology faculty are actively involved in departmental initiatives related to curriculum and assessment, student career preparation and professional development, and campus-wide committees. Biology faculty advise students in general biology and in specialized options focused on Biotechnology, Biomedical Sciences, Nuclear Medicine Technology, Marine Biology and Aquaculture, and Environmental Biology. In addition, the department teaches scientific reasoning courses for the General Education program and lab sciences support courses for allied health and sports and movement sciences departments. Salem State University is committed to excellence in teaching. We pride ourselves in providing first-rate classroom experiences and supervising intensive learning opportunities such as research and internships. Many of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, veterans, and adult learners. Salem State University is located in the Greater Boston area in the historic city of Salem, Massachusetts. The Greater Boston region is famous for its world-class education, healthcare, and business enterprises, and the area offers numerous opportunities for professional and personal enrichment. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours (approximately 4 lecture or lab sections) per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications PhD or equivalent in relevant discipline (e.g., biomedical sciences, physiology) or M.D. Experience teaching at the college/university level or in clinical settings Demonstrated interest to involve undergraduates in research both inside and outside the classroom using shared research spaces in the department Experience with engaging and inclusive pedagogies in lectures, lab, and/or online modalities Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to inclusive teaching and mentoring practices that resonate with and supports the success of undergraduates from diverse backgrounds Experience teaching both introductory and upper-level courses A desire to take an active role in supporting and advising students in Pre-Health pathways and/or the Nuclear Medicine Technology concentration As an emerging Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Salem State University seeks to enrich the faculty ranks by actively encouraging candidates whose lived and scholarly experiences directly address issues regarding the health, welfare, and representation of Latinx populations in the United States. Candidates who meet this strongly desired qualification should present documented activities in Latinx-related teaching, scholarship/research, and service, including community-based endeavors in each of these three areas Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. All applicants are encouraged to apply; however, Salem State University cannot guarantee that it will sponsor visas for individuals who are not otherwise authorized to work in the United States. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) e9d05718 Last Name (required) 6cd20af9 Email (required) 911f8a98 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5539af3c Last Name (required) 21c1e6c9 Email (required) 555f203a Job Alert 1d0e8aa4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 121 - Biology 121 - Biology Categories Faculty: Tenured Faculty: Tenured Employment Type Tenure-Track Tenure-Track Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 38432465 Last Name (required) 9f64f47a Email (required) d111442d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cooki