    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-biology-cell-biology-and-biochemistry-full-time-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Faculty: Biology (Cell Biology and Biochemistry), Full-Time, Tenure-Track -",
      "description": "Faculty: Biology (Cell Biology and Biochemistry), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Faculty: Biology (Cell Biology and Biochemistry), Full-Time, Tenure-Track - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Biology (Cell Biology and Biochemistry), Full-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty: Biology (Cell Biology and Biochemistry), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 492977 121 - Biology Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Overview The biology department invites applications for a full-time, tenure track faculty position in cell biology and biochemistry to begin September 2027. We seek a colleague who encourages student learning through innovative pedagogy and who has expertise in contemporary methods in cell biology and biochemistry. The successful candidate will have primary teaching responsibility in Cell Biology (a foundational course for majors), upper-level Biological Chemistry with a laboratory, and the opportunity to teach introductory biology. The ideal candidate will have plans for engaging undergraduate students in course-based and/or mentored research opportunities. We seek a collaborative colleague who cares deeply about supporting students and preparing future scientists and STEM professionals. Biology faculty are actively involved in departmental initiatives related to curriculum and assessment, student career preparation and professional development, and campus-wide committees. Biology faculty advise students in general biology and in specialized options focused on Biotechnology, Biomedical Sciences, Nuclear Medicine Technology, Marine Biology and Aquaculture, and Environmental Biology. In addition, the department teaches scientific reasoning courses for the General Education program and lab sciences support courses for allied health and sports and movement sciences departments. What makes Salem State University distinctive isn't just what happens in our classrooms. It's who's in them. Our students are ambitious, diverse and often the first in their families to pursue higher education. Our faculty rise to meet that with rigorous scholarship, thoughtful teaching and a genuine investment in student growth. We're the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University and a proud Hispanic and Minority-Serving Institution, designations we've earned and take seriously. If you're looking for a collegial academic home where your work truly matters, Salem State delivers. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications PhD or equivalent in a relevant discipline (e.g., cell biology, biochemistry) Experience teaching at the college/university level Demonstrated interest to involve undergraduates in research both inside and outside the classroom using shared research spaces in the department Experience with engaging and inclusive pedagogies in lectures, lab, and/or online modalities Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to inclusive teaching and mentoring practices that support the success of undergraduates from a variety of backgrounds and experiences Experience teaching both introductory and upper-level courses Expertise in bioinformatics, biostatistics, or programming languages (e.g., R, python) Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. All applicants are encouraged to apply; however, Salem State University cannot guarantee that it will sponsor visas for individuals who are not otherwise authorized to work in the United States. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) ce41ad66 Last Name (required) a0028f2c Email (required) b6de8dce Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 9eb6196a Last Name (required) 6e17cc7e Email (required) 4a5a41c3 Job Alert 1c5293f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 121 - Biology 121 - Biology Categories Faculty: Tenured Faculty: Tenured Employment Type Tenure-Track Tenure-Track Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 13c34428 Last Name (required) f2d1fef6 Email (required) ef172fe5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Performance Cookies Performance cookies are cookies used specifically for gathering data on how visitors use a website, which pages of a website are visited most often, or if they get error messages on web pages. These cookies monitor only the performance of the site as the user interacts with it. Manage Cookies I do 