    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-childhood-education-and-care-special-education-full-time-temporary-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 -",
      "description": "Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 - Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 Faculty: Childhood Education and Care, (Special Education), Full-Time, Temporary, Spring 2027 492982 443 - Childhood Education and Care Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Non-Tenure-Track (Temp) On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Overview Salem State University invites applications for a full-time, temporary faculty position in Special Education beginning in Spring 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic educator preparation program committed to inclusive practices, equity, and strong partnerships with schools and communities. At Salem State University, academic excellence and student success are at the heart of our mission. As a public university, we are dedicated to providing an inclusive and supportive environment that fosters our students' learning and growth. We seek faculty who share our values of collegiality, civic engagement and continuous improvement. Join us in a community where your commitment to scholarship and teaching will empower students to make meaningful contributions to society. Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, scholarship and contributions to continuously improve the department and university. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Required Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in Special Education or a closely related field (by time of appointment). Professional experience as a Special Education teacher. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive instructional practices in educational settings and culturally responsive practices. A scholarly agenda Strong organizational and written and communication skills Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Evidence-based instructional practices, materials, and methods for teaching students with moderate disabilities Literacy instruction for students with disabilities Diagnostic and educational assessment for students with disabilities Development, interpretation, and implementation of Individualized Education Programs (IEPs) Autism spectrum disorder, including school-based and home-based interventions, collaboration with families, and advocacy for students with autism Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in higher education. Experience with online asynchronous or hybrid instruction and learning management systems, such as Canvas. Working Location This is an on-site position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Application review will commence in September. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 9adb1d38