    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-secondary-and-higher-education-school-counseling-full-time-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice -",
      "description": "Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice - Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice Faculty: Secondary and Higher Education (School Counseling), Full-Time, Professor of Practice 492980 444 - Secondary and Higher Education Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Professor of Practice On-site $80,000 - $85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Overview The McKeown School of Education is seeking applicants for a full-time, professor of practice position with a specialization in School Counseling beginning in September 2027. The School Counseling Program prepares candidates to be educational leaders, social justice advocates, and system change agents with an emphasis on working in a variety of urban and suburban settings. This faculty member will teach a total of six graduate level classes per year, as well as advising school counseling students. Course topics may include: Multicultural Counseling, Career Counseling, Seminar in School Adjustment Counseling, and School Counseling practicum/seminar courses. Additional information about School Counseling Program can be found here: https://www.salemstate.edu/academics/mckeown-school-education/school-counseling/master-education-school-counseling Salem State University is a public institution with a clear sense of its mission: to provide an exceptional education that opens doors and transforms lives. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University, we foster partnerships between our campus and the communities we serve, and our faculty are essential to that work. Our scholars and educators believe in what they do and thrive in a supportive, inclusive academic environment. As a proud Hispanic and Minority-Serving Institution, we're proud of the students we serve and the community we've built around their success. Join a university where your research, your teaching and your values all have room to flourish. Please Note: This is a four year, fixed term position ending on May 31, 2031 . Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, and demonstrated consistent and substantive effort to maintaining modern skills and knowledge in their field of practice. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. This position will work collaboratively with the graduate program coordinator and the field office to facilitate program coordination. For the academic year 2027-2028, shared program coordination duties include: The direct supervision of school counseling candidates Conducting student admission reviews and new student onboarding Managing students’ plans of study Monitoring of internship and practicum site approval and accountability Reporting of hours Assisting with curriculum planning Maintaining records for a program with national reach. Required Qualifications An earned masters degree in school counseling or a related area Current licensure/certification as a practicing school counselor A minimum of three years of documented prior experience as a school counselor An understanding of the school adjustment counselor role Experience working with students through hybrid learning, mentoring, and training Membership in the American School Counseling Association Preferred Qualifications An earned PhD in Counselor Education from a CACREP-accredited program or PhD in Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited program Evidence of strong clinical skills and a strong school counselor identity Evidence of strong teaching skills at the undergraduate and graduate levels Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Application review will commence in September. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) ffbdf180 Last Name (required) 5bc655c0 Email (required) d01b9b17 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 679a0f39 Last Name (required) dc1680ec Email (required) 36284941 Job Alert b5ae32c9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 444 - Secondary and Higher Education 444 - Secondary and Higher Education Categories Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Employment Type Professor of Practice Professor of Practice Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) bcb944c3 Last Name (required) 1c8695c0 Email (required) 55c883ef Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Appli