    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/faculty-childhood-education-and-care-literacy-full-time-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice -",
      "description": "Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice - Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice - Kiosk mode Join our team Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice Faculty, Childhood Education and Care (Literacy), Full-Time, Professor of Practice 492985 443 - Childhood Education and Care Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Professor of Practice On-site $80,000-$85,000 (for the rank of assistant professor) Overview The Professor of Practice, Literacy is a non-tenure track faculty position focused on strengthening literacy instruction and clinical practice within educator preparation programs at Salem State. In addition to teaching literacy courses, this role centers on supervising teacher candidates, training and coaching other supervisors, and ensuring high-quality practicum experiences are aligned with state standards, with a particular emphasis on literacy across Early Childhood, Elementary, and Moderate Disabilities (PK–8) licensure programs. This position begins in Fall 2027. Salem State University is where scholarship meets purpose. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University, we believe education matters beyond the classroom, and our faculty are central to that mission. They bring intellectual curiosity and a genuine commitment to student success, teaching students who will go on to shape their communities, many of whom are the first in their families to earn a college degree. We value collaboration, academic rigor and the kind of civic-minded engagement that makes a real difference. If you're driven by meaningful work and want to be part of something bigger than any single course or semester, Salem State is your place. Please Note: This is a four year, fixed term position ending on May 31, 2031 . Duties and Responsibilities Candidates are required to perform duties in accordance with the MSCA contract . Duties include teaching, advising, and demonstrated consistent and substantive effort to maintaining modern skills and knowledge in their field of practice. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester. The position is subject to available funding. Specific Duties and Responsibilities Teach literacy related, DESE aligned education courses for teacher candidates in the Early Childhood, Elementary and Moderate Disabilities licensure programs. Supervise teacher candidates in practicum placements for Early Childhood, Elementary, and/or Moderate Disabilities (PK–8) licensure programs, with a focus on effective literacy instruction. Train, coach, support and provide feedback to practicum supervisors in observing and evaluating literacy instruction in alignment with Massachusetts Department of Elementary and Secondary Education (DESE) program approval expectations. Develop, deliver and evaluate professional learning for practicum supervisors to ensure consistency and quality in literacy-focused observation and feedback. Collaborate closely with the McKeown School of Education Office of Licensure and Field Engagement to support candidate success and the quality of pre-practicum and practicum placements aligned with DESE’s expectations for high quality instructional materials and evidence-based, culturally and linguistically sustaining literacy instruction. Collaborate with faculty in the McKeown School of Education on the content of literacy education courses. Support continuous program improvement efforts related to literacy and state approval standards. Maintain strong partnerships with schools and districts to support high-quality pre-practicum and practicum experiences. Required Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, Special Education, Literacy, or a closely related field. Reading Specialist license or PreK-2 or 1-6 Teacher license or Moderate Disabilities license (PreK-8) or a comparable license or an equivalent credential that demonstrates advanced literacy expertise. Significant professional experience (at least five years) teaching literacy. Demonstrated expertise in evidence-based literacy instruction and assessment. Experience mentoring, supervising, or coaching teacher candidates and/or practicing educators. Familiarity with Massachusetts DESE early literacy standards and program approval expectations. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in a relevant field. Prior experience training or supporting practicum supervisors or instructional coaches. Teaching experience in higher education and/or educator preparation programs. Strong collaboration and partnership-building skills with PK–12 schools and districts. Demonstrated technology skills, including the ability to use learning management systems, such as Canvas. Salem State University seeks faculty and librarians whose teaching, scholarship, and service will contribute to student success, academic excellence, and the university’s public mission. We welcome candidates with demonstrated ability to work effectively with students from varied backgrounds and to support an inclusive learning environment. Applicants may describe relevant accomplishments in teaching, scholarship/research, service, and community-engaged work. Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) ba936487 Last Name (required) 03dec358 Email (required) 6781e5c6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 032fe42a Last Name (required) e5e27b2a Email (required) 5455b777 Job Alert d5202c91 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 443 - Childhood Education and Care 443 - Childhood Education and Care Categories Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Faculty: Non-Tenured Not On Track Employment Type Professor of Practice Professor of Practice Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 00d3607a Last Name (required) c51c540a Email (required) 7de8b66a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Performance Cookies Performance cookies are cookies used specifically for gathering data on how visitors use a website, which pages of a website are visited most often, or if they get error messages on web pages. These cookies monitor only the performance of the site as the user interacts with it. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a working location"
