    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-faculty-day-nursing-public-health-ay-2025-2026-salem-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Day, Nursing, (Public Health), AY 2025-2026",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Day, Nursing, (Public Health), AY 2025-2026 - Salem, Massachusetts, United States Adjunct Faculty Day, Nursing, (Public Health), AY 2025-2026 - Salem, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Join our team Adjunct Faculty Day, Nursing, (Public Health), AY 2025-2026 Adjunct Faculty Day, Nursing, (Public Health), AY 2025-2026 492697 424 - Nursing Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time On-site $1,000 - $2,253.60 per Semester Hour Credit of Instruction Overview: Salem State University Nursing School of Nursing invites applications for adjunct faculty with interest and experience teaching Public Health in a clinical setting. Teaching assignments may include days, evenings, or weekends and range from 6 to 15 hours/week over the course of the semester. Duties and Responsibilities: Work collaboratively with faculty, in a school with future-directed leadership and a collective focus on academic excellence, success of our students and faculty development. • Provide weekly updates on student performance to the course coordinator. • Attend the mandatory program update meeting each semester for clinical adjunct faculty. • Attend orientation/training to fulfill compliance requirements as required by the School of Nursing and by any assigned clinical practice sites. • Be accountable for instruction, supervision, and evaluation of student competencies of a diverse student population in the clinical practice and/or laboratory setting. • Develop and maintain competence appropriate to teaching responsibilities including, but not limited to orientation and mentoring to the nurse educator role. • Participation in professional development in nursing education such as certification, and continuing education. • Collaborate with faculty, staff, and program administrator to support policies and objectives of the program and on all applicable components of the systematic evaluation plan. Required Qualifications: • Hold a current unencumbered Massachusetts Registered Nurse license. • Graduate degree in nursing. Minimum of five years of full-time registered nurse experience within the last eight years. Evidence of clinical competency in clinical instruction. OR • Hold a current unencumbered Massachusetts Registered Nurse license. • Possess a minimum of five years full-time registered nurse experience within the last eight years. • Baccalaureate degree in nursing and meet at least one of the following criteria 1. Matriculation in a graduate nursing program with expected graduation date within five years of the date of appointment. OR 2. Possess a related non-nursing graduate degree. OR 3. Possess a current Nurse Education Certification recognized by a Massachusetts Board certified organization. Preferred Qualifications: - - Teaching experience - Demonstrated commitment to collaboration and collegiality - Demonstrated commitment to teaching, supervision, and advising - Strength and potential for excellence and leadership in community engagement and university services - Appropriate terminal degree - College-level teaching experience, at both the undergraduate and graduate levels - Experience teaching a multicultural population Working Location: Clinical Adjunct Faculty are assigned a working location from North Shore to Boston. Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement: The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement: Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies: Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 8d6ba09c Last Name (required) 49faaaba Email (required) 80beda15 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 0d339171 Last Name (required) 38db1445 Email (required) 3816d6d9 Job Alert babcb0e9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 424 - Nursing 424 - Nursing Categories Faculty: Adjunct Faculty: Adjunct Employment Type Part-Time Part-Time Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) f387c233 Last Name (required) ec5079f2 Email (required) df6fede7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Cand