urse license. • Graduate degree in nursing. Minimum of five years of full-time registered nurse experience within the last eight years. Evidence of clinical competency in clinical instruction. OR • Hold a current unencumbered Massachusetts Registered Nurse license. • Possess a minimum of five years full-time registered nurse experience within the last eight years. • Baccalaureate degree in nursing and meet at least one of the following criteria 1. Matriculation in a graduate nursing program with expected graduation date within five years of the date of appointment. OR 2. Possess a related non-nursing graduate degree. OR 3. Possess a current Nurse Education Certification recognized by a Massachusetts Board certified organization. Preferred Qualifications: - - Teaching experience - Demonstrated commitment to collaboration and collegiality - Demonstrated commitment to teaching, supervision, and advising - Strength and potential for excellence and leadership in community engagement and university services - Appropriate terminal degree - College-level teaching experience, at both the undergraduate and graduate levels - Experience teaching a multicultural population Working Location: Clinical Adjunct Faculty are assigned a working location from North Shore to Boston. Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement: The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement: Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified app