      "title": "Adjunct Faculty (CE), Nursing, Clinical, (Mental Health) 2025-2026 -",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty (CE), Nursing, Clinical, (Mental Health) 2025-2026 - Adjunct Faculty (CE), Nursing, Clinical, (Mental Health) 2025-2026 - Kiosk mode Join our team Adjunct Faculty (CE), Nursing, Clinical, (Mental Health) 2025-2026 Adjunct Faculty (CE), Nursing, Clinical, (Mental Health) 2025-2026 492702 424 - Nursing Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Closing on: Sep 18 2028 On-site $1,610 - $1,987 per SHCI (Semester Hours of Credit Instruction) Overview: Salem State University Nursing School of Nursing invites applications for adjunct faculty with interest and experience teaching Mental Health in a clinical setting. Teaching assignments may include days, evenings, or weekends and range from 6 to 15 hours/week over the course of the semester. Duties and Responsibilities: Work collaboratively with faculty, in a school with future-directed leadership and a collective focus on academic excellence, success of our students and faculty development. Required Qualifications: Hold a current unencumbered Massachusetts Registered Nurse license. Graduate degree in nursing. Minimum of five years of full-time registered nurse experience within the last eight years. Evidence of clinical competency in clinical instruction. OR Hold a current unencumbered Massachusetts Registered Nurse license. Possess a minimum of five years full-time registered nurse experience within the last eight years. Baccalaureate degree in nursing and meet at least one of the following criteria Matriculation in a graduate nursing program with expected graduation date within five years of the date of appointment. OR Possess a related non-nursing graduate degree. OR Possess a current Nurse Education Certification recognized by a Massachusetts Board certified organization. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated commitment to collaboration and collegiality Demonstrated commitment to teaching, supervision, and advising Strength and potential for excellence and leadership in community engagement and u