    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/adjunct-faculty-graduate-mckeown-school-of-education-school-adjustment-counseling-ay-2025-2026": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Graduate, McKeown School of Education, School Adjustment Counseling, AY 2025-2026 -",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Graduate, McKeown School of Education, School Adjustment Counseling, AY 2025-2026 - Adjunct Faculty Graduate, McKeown School of Education, School Adjustment Counseling, AY 2025-2026 - Kiosk mode Join our team Adjunct Faculty Graduate, McKeown School of Education, School Adjustment Counseling, AY 2025-2026 Adjunct Faculty Graduate, McKeown School of Education, School Adjustment Counseling, AY 2025-2026 492573 444 - Secondary and Higher Education Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Closing on: Jun 30 2028 On-site $1,610 - $1,987 per SHCI (Semester Hours of Credit Instruction) Overview: Salem State University is seeking part-time adjunct faculty with interest and experience teaching graduate-level school counseling and school adjustment counseling classes. Teaching and supervision assignments will depend upon the expertise of the candidate and the needs of the program. Classes and supervision may be in-person, fully online, or hybrid, depending on the department's needs. Priority will be given to candidates who can teach in a variety of modalities, including in-person and fully online. Occasionally, sections include high school students taking college courses through the Salem State Early College program, so experience working with high school students is highly desirable. Duties and Responsibilities: - Teach graduate level school counseling and/or school adjustment counseling courses. - Supervise candidates in their pre-practicum and/or practicum setting. - Work collaboratively with faculty, in a school with future-directed leadership and a collective focus on academic excellence, success of our students and faculty development. Required Qualifications: Master's degree Teaching experience Demonstrated commitment to collaboration and collegiality Demonstrated commitment to teaching, supervision, and advising Strength and potential for excellence and leadership in community engagement and university services Preferred Qualifications Appropriate terminal degree College-level teaching experience, at both the undergraduate and graduate levels Experience teaching a multicultural population Working Location: This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with some on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions: Please apply online and attach CV, cover letter, and transcripts. To ensure you are assigned the highest eligible rank, you should provide the total sum of credits you have taught at the college/university level. This information can be added to your CV, cover letter, or a separate document Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement: The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. Apply now First Name (required) 2252e52d Last Name (required) 5918068a Email (required) a5c6f845 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track CIS Executive Functioning and Employment Coach 493085 584 - Community of Inclusive Scholar Staff: Administrator/Professional Part-Time Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track S