    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-director-of-the-nursing-resource-center": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center -",
      "description": "Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center - Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center - Kiosk mode Join our team Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center 493086 578 - Nursing Resource Center Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $82,000-$88,000 Overview The School of Nursing prepares the next generation of nurses to lead with skill, compassion, and clinical confidence. The Nursing Resource Center sits at the heart of that mission — and the Assistant Director who helps run it shapes the hands-on learning environment where students move from classroom theory to clinical readiness. In this role, you will oversee the day-to-day operations of the Nursing Resource Center, including simulation lab scheduling, equipment management, and staff coordination. You will design, facilitate, and evaluate simulation-based learning experiences aligned with current nursing curriculum and accreditation standards, working closely with nursing faculty to ensure skills lab activities connect meaningfully with didactic and clinical coursework. You will also supervise lab staff and student workers, providing ongoing guidance, training, and performance feedback to maintain a high-functioning, student-ready environment. What you do at Salem State University matters. As a staff member, you'll be part of an institution that is a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution and that serves one of the most diverse student bodies in Massachusetts. We believe in building a workplace culture that mirrors our values: inclusive, equitable and driven by a genuine desire to help people succeed. You'll find professional development opportunities, a supportive team environment and work that connects directly to our students' futures. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) preferred; BSN with relevant experience considered Active, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license Experience in clinical nursing education, simulation, or clinical coordination Preferred Qualifications Experience with clinical placement systems (e.g., CCP) Experience with simulation-based education Experience in higher education or academic settings Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Recommended jobs Nurse Practitioner 493107 150 - Counseling And Health Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus 