    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/nurse-practitioner-7920ffd8-4b3b-4329-a67e-aa2b4407118a": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner -",
      "description": "Nurse Practitioner - Nurse Practitioner - Kiosk mode Join our team Nurse Practitioner Nurse Practitioner 493107 150 - Counseling And Health Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time On-site $90,000 - $95,000 Overview The Nurse Practitioner assesses, diagnoses, and treats student health problems within established primary care protocols; and plans and presents health education programming to increase campus health promotion and wellness, as delivered in the student health services at Salem State University. While the preferred schedule is Monday through Friday, 8:30am-5:00pm, flexibility in scheduling may be considered to meet departmental and employee needs. Counseling and Health Services is a multidisciplinary office that includes confidential counseling, health, and prevention services to the university community of students. The health center staff function to foster interpersonal development and address actual and potential health issues that create barriers to student success. A wide spectrum of medical services are provided by health center staff. They include a focus on illness, injury, episodic and urgent care, reproductive health, immunizations, health promotion and prevention, outreach, and wellness. Health staff are committed to supporting an environment that is culturally inclusive, and recognizes diversity and personal development of our students, staff, faculty, and community partners. A commitment to quality improvement and assessment are essential to this role. Salem State University is where professional ambition and community purpose meet. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University and a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution, we have a deep commitment to the students, employees and neighbors who make up our university community. Our staff are integral to everything we do, from supporting first-generation college students to advancing civic engagement across the North Shore. If you're looking for a career that challenges and fulfills you, and a team that celebrates who you are, we'd love to welcome you to Salem State. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) degree from an accredited school/college of nursing Licensure to practice in Massachusetts as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN), including current DPH prescriptive authority and DEA licensure. Experience working with an adolescent or young adult population. Proof of current and active malpractice insurance. Possess current certification in Basic Life Support for healthcare providers. Possess or eligible to obtain insurance credentialing in order to be able to bill health insurance for services provided at Salem State University health services. Familiarity with HIPPAA and FERPA privacy and confidentiality requirements and compliance. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated leadership or supervisory experience, including mentoring or managing student employees, interns, or support staff within a healthcare or educational environment Experience in health education or wellness programming, including the ability to design and implement outreach initiatives that promote preventative care and student well-being Program management support, including data tracking, grant-related activities, or oversight of health-related access improvement programs Proficiency in Spanish to enhance communication, cultural responsiveness, and accessibility of health services Understanding of and commitment to a reproductive justice framework, including the ability to provide inclusive, affirming care Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with on-campus, in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume and cover letter. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. We recognize that candidates may hesitate to apply if they do not meet every listed qualification. We value diverse experiences and perspectives. If you believe your skills, experience, and enthusiasm align with this opportunity, we encourage you to apply and share what you can bring to Salem State University Counseling and Health Services.\" or \"Research shows that some candidates apply only when they meet every qualification. We value diverse experiences and perspectives. If you're interested in the role and meet several of the requirements, we encourage you to apply and tell us how you can contribute to Salem State University Counseling and Health Services. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 680ef240 Last Name (required) 3ed0bb6a Email (required) 429cd81e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center 493086 578 - Nursing Resource Center Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Assistant Director of Outreach and Community Engagement 493088 243 - School Of Social Work Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Group Exercise Instructor 493081 684 - Campus LIfe / Recreation Admin Staff: Temporary/Contract Part-Time Faculty: Computer Science, (Software Engineering and Cloud Computing), Full-Time, Tenure-Track 493094 140 - Computer Science Dept Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 86cd4335 Last Name (required) 937cf63e Email (required) e2b5c20a Job Alert 8cb72a17 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 150 - Counseling And Health 150 - Counseling And Health Categories Staff: Administrator/Professional Staff: Administrator/Professional Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 2d61e319 Last Name (required) 49216aab Email (required) 38661d99 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Performance Cookies Performance cookies are cookies used specifically for gathering data on how visitor