    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/administrative-assistant-ii-msoe-and-program-support": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II, MSOE and Program Support -",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II, MSOE and Program Support - Administrative Assistant II, MSOE and Program Support - Kiosk mode Join our team Administrative Assistant II, MSOE and Program Support Administrative Assistant II, MSOE and Program Support 493146 568 - Education-Deans Office Staff: Classified/Hourly Part-Time Closing on: Oct 31 2026 Hybrid $32,524.93 annually / $1,250.96 biweekly Overview The McKeown School of Education (MSOE) Administrative Assistant II (AAII) supports daily operations of the school. The MSOE administrative assistant works closely with the MSOE Office Manager and collaborates with administrative staff and faculty to ensure that the MSOE functions effectively in fulfilling its mission to provide students with high-quality education. At Salem State University, every role on campus plays a part in something meaningful. As a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution, we've built a culture that reflects the diversity of the students and communities we serve, and we bring that same spirit to our workplace. You'll find colleagues who are collaborative, students who are motivated and a mission you can stand behind. Whether you're just starting your career or bringing years of experience, Salem State is a place where your contributions count. Please Note: This is a part-time, benefited position working 19.5 hours per week. Required Qualifications Applicants must have at least (A) three years of full-time, or equivalent part-time, experience in office management, office administration, business administration or business management, the major duties of which included one or more of the following functions: purchasing, personnel management, budgeting, accounting, records management, work simplification, grants management, contract administration or program management, or (B) any equivalent combination of the required experience and the substitutions below. Substitutions: I. An Associate’s or higher degree with a major in business administration, business management or public administration may be substituted for a maximum of two years of the required experience.* II. An Associate’s or higher degree with a major other than in business administration, business management or public administration may be substituted for a maximum of one year of the required experience.* *Education toward such a degree will be prorated on the basis of the proportion of the requirements actually completed. Preferred Qualifications A bachelor's degree Previous professional experience in a higher education setting Strong time management skills and ability to organize, prioritize and complete multiple tasks simultaneously with close attention to detail in order to meet deadlines Technical knowledge and the ability to develop and maintain appropriate systems and databases to support office operations are necessary Experience using PeopleSoft, CFRS, Fusion and Procard systems and knowledge of current software packages such as MS Word, Access, Excel and PowerPoint Working Location This is a hybrid position in Salem, MA with some on-campus, in-person responsibilities. Application Instructions Please apply online. Resume and cover letter are not required, but are appreciated. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) 308ad0b3 Last Name (required) 0b81f85b Email (required) 7b570608 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer 493158 223 - HR Department Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Maintainer I and II (Multiple Openings) 492997 153 - Custodial Service Staff: Classified/Hourly Full-Time Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center 493086 578 - Nursing Resource Center Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Nurse Practitioner 493107 150 - Counseling And Health Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Performance Cookies Performance cookies are cookies used specifically for gathering data on how visitors use a website, which pages of a website are visited most often, or if they get error messages on web pag