    "https://salem-state-university.career-pages.com/jobs/assistant-vice-president-chief-human-resources-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer -",
      "description": "Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer - Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer - Kiosk mode Join our team Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer 493158 223 - HR Department Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 On-site $170,000-$180,000 Overview The Assistant Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer (AVP, CHRO) is responsible for providing strategic leadership in all aspects of the human resources function across the institution, helps drive a culture of change, and makes meaningful contributions throughout the campus community. Working collaboratively with leaders across the campus, the AVP will oversee an effective, responsive, and customer service-oriented operation, and develop strategic programs and innovative practices in support of the university’s mission. The AVP will promote a high-performing, positive, equitable, and productive culture, with the goals of maintaining high levels of employee engagement while fostering an inclusive and collegial environment. The AVP is responsible for the university’s human resources policies and procedures; employee relations and labor relations, including administration of the APA and AFSCME collective bargaining agreements; providing support to the President and Provost in administration of the MSCA collective bargaining agreement; recruitment, employee education, training and professional development; salary structure design (non-union), compensation and administration, including classification of new positions and performance management and all other matters relating to the human resources function. Salem State University is where professional ambition and community purpose meet. As the Commonwealth's Civic Engagement University and a proud Hispanic-Serving Institution, we have a deep commitment to the students, employees and neighbors who make up our university community. Our staff are integral to everything we do, from supporting first-generation college students to advancing civic engagement across the North Shore. If you're looking for a career that challenges and fulfills you, and a team that celebrates who you are, we'd love to welcome you to Salem State. Required Qualifications A bachelor’s degree in human resources or a related field Ten years of experience working in human resources in positions of increasing responsibility Experience managing human resources staff Experience managing budgets Preferred Qualifications Three years of experience in labor and employee relations Experience working in higher education or a similarly complex organization Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Knowledge of Commonwealth of Massachusetts laws, systems, and policies Strong project management, organizational, and planning skills and the ability to effectively prioritize and solve complex problems while making decisions Working Location This is an onsite position in Salem, MA with in-person responsibilities, which may require occasional work on evenings and weekends. Application Instructions Please apply online and attach resume, cover letter. Please submit your application by November 15, 2026. Employment is contingent upon a completed background and CORI check satisfactory to the university. This position is not eligible for H1B visa sponsorship. EEO Statement The university considers all qualified candidates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability status, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, genetic information, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition or any other characteristic protected by law. ADA Statement Salem State University complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities. For accommodation information or requests please email eo-hr@salemstate.edu . Recruitment Agencies Salem State University does not partner with or accept candidates from outside staffing agencies. All hiring is managed directly by our internal Talent Acquisition team. Apply now First Name (required) a4090841 Last Name (required) a944f024 Email (required) 4f03f5c8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Administrative Assistant II, MSOE and Program Support 493146 568 - Education-Deans Office Staff: Classified/Hourly Part-Time Maintainer I and II (Multiple Openings) 492997 153 - Custodial Service Staff: Classified/Hourly Full-Time Assistant Director of the Nursing Resource Center 493086 578 - Nursing Resource Center Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Nurse Practitioner 493107 150 - Counseling And Health Staff: Administrator/Professional Full-Time Adjunct Faculty Graduate, Psychology, Counseling, AY 2026-2027 493151 234 - Psychology Faculty: Adjunct Part-Time Faculty, Nursing (Adult Health), Full Time, Tenure Track, AY 2027-2028 493122 424 - Nursing Faculty: Tenured Tenure-Track Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 2f55820b Last Name (required) 25fbdf3b Email (required) 3503bebe Job Alert de4e6671 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 223 - HR Department 223 - HR Department Categories Staff: Administrator/Professional Staff: Administrator/Professional Employment Type Full-Time Full-Time Working location On-site On-site Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) c2242e73 Last Name (required) 70a1f301 Email (required) 2c70a0b6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. You can view our university policies here . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Technical and functional cookies are required for the Website to work. These include, for example, session management, Website security, shopping cart, language preferences, app launch, app management, or API (Application Program Interface) management. Performance Cookies Performance cookies are cookies used specifically for gathering data on how visitors use a website, which pages of a website are visited most often, or if they get error messages on web pages. These cookies monitor only the performance of the site as the user interacts with it. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a working location"
